WEBVTT

STYLE
::cue(c.color9CD5FF) { color: #9CD5FF; }

1
00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:07.000 line:5% align:center
<b><c.color9CD5FF>One Pace Addon</c></b>

2
00:03:01.490 --> 00:03:04.870
<b>Windmill Village,
East Blue</b>

3
00:03:05.250 --> 00:03:06.210
How is that possible?

4
00:03:06.210 --> 00:03:08.460
They left Garp on Pirate Island?

5
00:03:08.460 --> 00:03:09.880
What happened to him?

6
00:03:09.880 --> 00:03:13.380
The article says he went there
to rescue some guy named Koby.

7
00:03:13.380 --> 00:03:16.260
I guess he succeeded.
Too bad it cost him his life.

8
00:03:16.260 --> 00:03:18.140
Where does it say he's dead?

9
00:03:18.510 --> 00:03:21.510
The man's a living legend.
This isn't how he's gonna go.

10
00:03:21.510 --> 00:03:23.220
Wipe those looks off your faces.

11
00:03:23.220 --> 00:03:25.270
You're right. I'm sure he's fine.

12
00:03:25.270 --> 00:03:26.770
Damn right he is.

13
00:03:29.770 --> 00:03:32.450
Who's laughing? You think this is funny?

14
00:03:34.860 --> 00:03:35.950
Oh, sweetheart.

15
00:03:36.570 --> 00:03:38.450
Don't worry. He didn't mean it.

16
00:03:38.450 --> 00:03:39.570
There, there.

17
00:03:39.570 --> 00:03:41.330
Oh, it was just the baby.

18
00:03:41.330 --> 00:03:42.540
I'm sorry, Makino.

19
00:03:43.290 --> 00:03:46.160
You're worried about Garp too, aren't you?

20
00:03:46.160 --> 00:03:50.170
Was that what you were laughing at?
You know Luffy's face now, don't you?

21
00:03:47.370 --> 00:03:49.580
"Straw Hats' Hostage Situation"

22
00:03:50.170 --> 00:03:52.960
We love Luffy. Yes, we do.

23
00:03:56.170 --> 00:03:58.010
What the hell are those idiots thinking?

24
00:04:03.310 --> 00:04:07.600
<b>Hostage Situation</b>

25
00:04:16.360 --> 00:04:17.860
Oh, we got a big one!

26
00:04:22.370 --> 00:04:24.330
<b>East Blue</b>

27
00:04:23.030 --> 00:04:24.330
It's an earthquake!

28
00:04:31.710 --> 00:04:34.210
<b>South Blue</b>

29
00:04:33.170 --> 00:04:35.550
– It's a tsunami!
– It's a tsunami!

30
00:04:35.550 --> 00:04:37.130
Get to high ground!

31
00:04:37.130 --> 00:04:39.130
<b>West Blue</b>

32
00:04:38.130 --> 00:04:40.090
Follow me! We have to go!

33
00:04:42.550 --> 00:04:44.640
<b>North Blue</b>

34
00:04:45.310 --> 00:04:46.350
What's happening?

35
00:04:47.890 --> 00:04:56.980
<b>The earthquake on that day
was unprecedented in recorded history.


It left severe damage
in its wake across the world.</b>

36
00:04:48.120 --> 00:04:52.520
The earthquake on that day was unlike
any other in recorded history.

37
00:04:52.520 --> 00:04:56.980
It caused devastating damage
all around the world.

38
00:04:57.990 --> 00:04:59.950
<b>Grand Line</b>

39
00:05:06.870 --> 00:05:09.660
Run for it!

40
00:05:10.250 --> 00:05:11.290
We're too late.

41
00:05:17.630 --> 00:05:22.050
The situation was highly unusual.
The earthquake's epicenter could not be detected.

42
00:05:22.430 --> 00:05:24.470
The truth was hidden from the public.

43
00:05:24.890 --> 00:05:28.850
But it was no coincidence that the tragedy
occurred six days after the Kingdom of Lulusia

44
00:05:28.850 --> 00:05:32.310
was wiped off the map
by the World Government.

45
00:05:31.350 --> 00:05:33.860
I'm at the remains of Lulusia!

46
00:05:34.480 --> 00:05:36.320
There is no trace of the land anymore!

47
00:05:36.320 --> 00:05:38.900
Just a giant hole swallowing up the sea!

48
00:05:39.240 --> 00:05:41.070
No further approach is possible!

49
00:05:41.070 --> 00:05:43.540
The hole isn't filling!

50
00:05:45.160 --> 00:05:52.390
Across the entire world, sea levels rose by approximately
one meter following the havoc of the earthquake.

51
00:05:54.170 --> 00:05:56.340
The beach has never flooded like this!

52
00:06:00.970 --> 00:06:03.970
At this rate, there won't
be any beach left here at all.

53
00:06:03.970 --> 00:06:05.850
Why isn't the tide pulling back?

54
00:06:05.850 --> 00:06:07.310
This is too cruel!

55
00:06:08.060 --> 00:06:11.560
Running on the beach is our favorite pastime!

56
00:06:12.350 --> 00:06:14.190
Give it back!

57
00:06:14.190 --> 00:06:17.810
This isn't glamorous at all!

58
00:06:18.320 --> 00:06:21.530
A number of beaches
have disappeared from the world.

59
00:06:21.530 --> 00:06:24.030
along with several islands.

60
00:06:26.570 --> 00:06:28.700
There's nothing left for us!

61
00:06:28.700 --> 00:06:31.660
We have to go! Sharks
swam right into my house!

62
00:06:33.410 --> 00:06:35.830
It's not supposed to be high tide yet.

63
00:06:35.830 --> 00:06:37.840
Might make for a big catch, though.

64
00:06:37.840 --> 00:06:40.090
You really want to go sailing in this mess?

65
00:06:42.840 --> 00:06:45.380
Sir, an update on the flooding situation.

66
00:06:46.510 --> 00:06:48.890
Sea levels are rising around the world.

67
00:06:49.430 --> 00:06:50.430
Yes, sir,

68
00:06:50.430 --> 00:06:52.310
but the cause is unclear.

69
00:06:53.680 --> 00:06:56.900
Meanwhile, Egghead.
was surrounded by a fleet

70
00:06:56.900 --> 00:07:01.360
of 100 Navy vessels of various sizes,
including twenty massive battleships.

71
00:07:01.360 --> 00:07:03.820
This was a force that could level a nation

72
00:07:03.820 --> 00:07:07.870
with power far exceeding
even that of a Buster Call.

73
00:07:08.490 --> 00:07:12.110
The total number of Marines was 30,000.

74
00:07:12.620 --> 00:07:16.170
And the leaders of this unprecedented operation.

75
00:07:21.090 --> 00:07:25.050
were nine Navy HQ vice admirals.

76
00:07:30.740 --> 00:07:34.480
and Admiral Kizaru.

77
00:07:36.440 --> 00:07:38.440
We're under attack!

78
00:08:14.470 --> 00:08:15.100
Hey!

79
00:08:15.980 --> 00:08:19.560
I told you not to attack
the Sea Beast Weapons!

80
00:08:19.560 --> 00:08:23.770
I heard you, but I'm afraid it attacked us first.

81
00:08:24.820 --> 00:08:26.740
Your meal, Kizaru, sir.

82
00:08:28.110 --> 00:08:30.530
Oh! My favorite!

83
00:08:30.910 --> 00:08:31.990
There you go!

84
00:08:31.990 --> 00:08:33.660
Eat it while it's hot!

85
00:08:40.670 --> 00:08:45.210
I gotta say, you're really putting me
on the spot here, Sentomaru.

86
00:08:46.130 --> 00:08:49.880
Why don't you just surrender
and have a nice bowl of ramen with me?

87
00:08:49.880 --> 00:08:53.220
Get serious. Attack again and we'll open fire.

88
00:08:53.220 --> 00:08:55.720
Oh, now you're scaring me.

89
00:08:55.720 --> 00:09:02.100
You know what you're up against here?
Punk developed the Pacifista's lasers by studying your power.

90
00:09:02.100 --> 00:09:04.270
Wow, so cool!

91
00:09:05.610 --> 00:09:09.360
Now you're here to murder him.
Never thought things would turn out this way.

92
00:09:09.740 --> 00:09:16.240
He studied the Void Century, Sentomaru.
Old friend or not, I can't defend a crime like that.

93
00:09:16.240 --> 00:09:17.580
In the end,

94
00:09:18.040 --> 00:09:19.960
I'm just the Navy's puppet.

95
00:09:21.420 --> 00:09:25.920
That said, we don't want to have this battle
any more than you do. The more we

96
00:09:25.920 --> 00:09:28.920
destroy, the more we lose.

97
00:09:28.920 --> 00:09:33.260
I was really hoping Lucci would clean this up
quickly without trashing the place.

98
00:09:33.260 --> 00:09:35.680
You can thank the Straw Hats for that one.

99
00:09:35.720 --> 00:09:39.640
<b>On a Battleship...</b>

100
00:09:40.810 --> 00:09:43.650
Don't let anyone else know I'm here.

101
00:09:43.650 --> 00:09:44.610
Yes, sir.

102
00:09:45.060 --> 00:09:50.070
"Straw Hats took Vegapunk hostage
and barricaded themselves inside."

103
00:09:50.070 --> 00:09:51.740
I like this article.

104
00:09:52.320 --> 00:09:53.700
It's Morgan's work.

105
00:09:54.320 --> 00:09:55.530
And what is the truth?

106
00:09:56.030 --> 00:09:59.500
Sir, we haven't received word
that CP0 has completed their mission.

107
00:10:00.540 --> 00:10:03.460
Sentomaru is prepared
to defend the island outside,

108
00:10:03.920 --> 00:10:06.420
so we can guess who's in the Labophase.

109
00:10:07.000 --> 00:10:10.340
First, we have Dr. Vegapunk, along
with his six satellites.

110
00:10:11.050 --> 00:10:14.140
They should have the four Seraphim protecting them.

111
00:10:14.140 --> 00:10:19.390
Then there's Straw Hat Luffy and his crew,
who seem to have allied with the doctor.

112
00:10:22.350 --> 00:10:28.770
Also, there's CP0's Rob Lucci, along
with the others in his leading unit, Kaku and Stussy.

113
00:10:28.770 --> 00:10:33.740
As for the other Cipher Pol agents, they appear
to have been captured by Sentomaru and his Pacifistas

114
00:10:33.740 --> 00:10:36.660
in the Fabriophase.

115
00:10:37.530 --> 00:10:42.790
One added note. The Frontier Dome
barrier status is currently at 100%,

116
00:10:42.790 --> 00:10:46.250
meaning that no one can enter
or leave the Labophase.

117
00:10:46.250 --> 00:10:52.300
It's been like that for an entire day.
We still don't know what's going on inside.

118
00:10:52.920 --> 00:10:57.850
What happened to all the researches
and technicians who were employed on Egghead?

119
00:10:58.220 --> 00:11:01.270
They're not present.
They evacuated the island yesterday.

120
00:11:01.640 --> 00:11:03.560
We've already located their ships.

121
00:11:03.560 --> 00:11:06.230
And what if they know too much?

122
00:11:06.980 --> 00:11:08.690
Sink them at once.

123
00:11:08.690 --> 00:11:09.440
Yes, sir!

124
00:11:10.480 --> 00:11:12.610
Just one more thing first.

125
00:11:12.610 --> 00:11:16.740
We spotted Jewelry Bonney.
She may be there with the Straw Hats.

126
00:11:16.740 --> 00:11:18.450
Kuma's daughter, you say?

127
00:11:18.990 --> 00:11:20.830
We have no more use for her.

128
00:11:21.440 --> 00:11:25.620
Forget about her. She's just a girl. Yes, sir.

129
00:11:29.130 --> 00:11:29.960
Admiral, sir.

130
00:11:32.240 --> 00:11:36.130
What? I'm trying to enjoy a meal here.

131
00:11:36.130 --> 00:11:39.410
We're picking up
a signal from Egghead. A signal?

132
00:11:39.760 --> 00:11:41.760
They seem to be making a call somewhere.

133
00:11:41.760 --> 00:11:44.230
We'll find out who they're calling then.

134
00:11:48.690 --> 00:11:49.610
It's Marie Jois.

135
00:11:49.650 --> 00:11:51.980
<b>Mary Geoise
The Holy Land</b>

136
00:11:55.320 --> 00:11:56.650
Who is this?

137
00:11:57.240 --> 00:12:01.030
Admiral, you should have
a black transponder snail on your wrist.

138
00:12:01.280 --> 00:12:04.040
Oh! You can tap the call. Whoa.

139
00:12:13.960 --> 00:12:15.420
Yeah. Hello?! It's me!

140
00:12:15.420 --> 00:12:16.920
York!

141
00:12:16.920 --> 00:12:18.050
You're still alive?

142
00:12:18.050 --> 00:12:19.760
That's all you have to say?

143
00:12:19.760 --> 00:12:21.010
Are you punky kidding me?

144
00:12:21.010 --> 00:12:24.100
Why the hell are you trying to kill me, too?!

145
00:12:22.140 --> 00:12:27.270
<b>Room of Authority</b>

146
00:12:24.100 --> 00:12:27.270
I'm the one who told you what Stella did!
Remember that, Peepaws?!

147
00:12:27.770 --> 00:12:32.020
Be that as it may, you're still
a Vegapunk, just like the others.

148
00:12:32.360 --> 00:12:35.320
I don't give a shit about the Void Century.

149
00:12:35.320 --> 00:12:39.170
And even if I did, you think I would have
tipped you off about it?!

150
00:12:39.450 --> 00:12:41.080
Use your brains!

151
00:12:41.910 --> 00:12:43.280
Fair enough.

152
00:12:43.280 --> 00:12:45.160
But how did you survive?

153
00:12:45.160 --> 00:12:47.370
Did CP0 fail at their mission?

154
00:12:47.960 --> 00:12:50.790
And what is the status of the Straw Hats?

155
00:12:52.750 --> 00:12:54.840
Well, I'm still here.

156
00:12:54.840 --> 00:12:56.800
That alone should tell you how the others are!

157
00:12:57.550 --> 00:13:00.180
I'm the one calling the shots now!

158
00:13:01.500 --> 00:13:05.140
Egghead is mine! All mine!

159
00:13:06.060 --> 00:13:07.850
You know what that means?

160
00:13:08.930 --> 00:13:11.350
If you skin bags try to backstab me again,

161
00:13:12.060 --> 00:13:15.910
I call the big gun!

162
00:13:20.820 --> 00:13:22.280
All four Seraphim!

163
00:13:25.260 --> 00:13:29.200
Now, about your little fleet
surrounding the island.

164
00:13:29.710 --> 00:13:32.000
You trying to start
a war with me or something?

165
00:13:32.460 --> 00:13:35.630
We could be convinced
to alter our plans, York.

166
00:13:37.340 --> 00:13:41.880
But let me confirm one thing first.
Can you create the Mother Flame yourself?

167
00:13:47.310 --> 00:13:49.480
Oh, now they want to negotiate!

168
00:13:49.480 --> 00:13:52.140
I'm glad I sent you that sample.

169
00:13:52.140 --> 00:13:54.670
I knew you'd get hooked
once you had a piece.

170
00:13:54.730 --> 00:13:56.900
It is of the highest priority.

171
00:13:57.510 --> 00:13:59.860
Whose priority, I wonder?

172
00:13:59.860 --> 00:14:02.860
Too bad! This island's the only power plant that makes it.

173
00:14:13.000 --> 00:14:14.040
Here's the sitch.

174
00:14:15.420 --> 00:14:19.380
Promise that me and the lab will make it out
of this thing unscathed.

175
00:14:19.760 --> 00:14:20.800
Agreed.

176
00:14:21.170 --> 00:14:23.550
And make me a Celestial Dragon
while you're at it!

177
00:14:23.550 --> 00:14:25.260
It shall be done.

178
00:14:25.760 --> 00:14:28.220
Then we've got ourselves a deal!

179
00:14:28.220 --> 00:14:30.430
One more thing.

180
00:14:31.680 --> 00:14:34.650
I need you to come and save me!

181
00:14:34.650 --> 00:14:39.900
Straw Hat Luffy is here!
And he's gonna kill me!

182
00:14:40.360 --> 00:14:41.280
– What?
– What?

183
00:14:41.280 --> 00:14:42.150
What's this?

184
00:14:42.150 --> 00:14:43.860
What's going on in there?

185
00:14:47.120 --> 00:14:48.660
Hey, Luffy.

186
00:14:48.660 --> 00:14:50.870
What should we do with this one?

187
00:14:50.870 --> 00:14:52.620
No more use for her now, right?

188
00:14:54.870 --> 00:14:59.590
No! No! Please!

189
00:15:00.130 --> 00:15:02.760
What a disaster this has been!

190
00:15:02.760 --> 00:15:04.840
I've caused you all such trouble, sorry.

191
00:15:04.840 --> 00:15:09.100
We forgive you. But she's a different story.

192
00:15:09.100 --> 00:15:11.790
So, Luffy, what's the plan for her?

193
00:15:13.060 --> 00:15:15.560
They want to keep her alive, right?

194
00:15:15.560 --> 00:15:17.940
Let's use her as a shield when we run away.

195
00:15:17.940 --> 00:15:20.360
So it's like a hostage case, huh?

196
00:15:21.150 --> 00:15:23.280
Talk to me, doc. Is she gonna be okay?

197
00:15:23.280 --> 00:15:27.990
It'll take time for her wounds to heal,
but with plenty of rest, she'll be fine.

198
00:15:29.950 --> 00:15:32.410
Hello?!

199
00:15:34.620 --> 00:15:35.370
My name is...

200
00:15:35.750 --> 00:15:37.750
Monkey D. Luffy!

201
00:15:37.750 --> 00:15:40.000
And I'm gonna be King of the Pirates!

202
00:15:40.000 --> 00:15:42.590
Is what you choose to open with?
What is wrong with you?

203
00:15:42.920 --> 00:15:47.130
We have Dr. Vegapunk!
All the Vegapunks even!

204
00:15:47.130 --> 00:15:49.260
If you wanna save York's

205
00:15:49.260 --> 00:15:53.470
life, clear all your ships
from the shore! Every last one!

206
00:15:53.470 --> 00:15:55.230
You don't understand!

207
00:15:55.230 --> 00:15:57.690
Straw Hat is a monster!

208
00:15:59.310 --> 00:16:00.560
He's torturing her!

209
00:16:00.560 --> 00:16:03.280
The rumors are true! He's a menace!

210
00:16:03.320 --> 00:16:05.860
<b>World Economic News</b>

211
00:16:04.280 --> 00:16:05.860
What is he doing?!

212
00:16:05.860 --> 00:16:08.240
No, Luffy. Why?

213
00:16:08.240 --> 00:16:09.820
That story was fake!

214
00:16:10.410 --> 00:16:12.620
So you're Straw Hat Luffy, are you?

215
00:16:12.620 --> 00:16:17.160
Have you suffered any casualties in the lab?
Who is still there with you?

216
00:16:17.230 --> 00:16:18.430
Huh?

217
00:16:18.540 --> 00:16:21.960
Well, let me see.
A couple people are hurt and.

218
00:16:21.960 --> 00:16:23.420
Clank.

219
00:16:26.720 --> 00:16:28.470
A woman's voice.

220
00:16:28.880 --> 00:16:30.640
Must be Nico Robin.

221
00:16:30.640 --> 00:16:32.760
Why'd you make me hang up?!

222
00:16:32.760 --> 00:16:34.640
Intel is a weapon.

223
00:16:34.640 --> 00:16:36.520
You must never give it to your enemies.

224
00:16:37.270 --> 00:16:38.600
Oh, right. Sorry.

225
00:16:38.980 --> 00:16:41.100
But hey. The ships will be gone now!

226
00:16:41.100 --> 00:16:42.310
Like hell they will!

227
00:16:42.690 --> 00:16:44.980
You think the Navy's that dumb?!

228
00:16:46.990 --> 00:16:48.490
What's our next move?

229
00:16:48.490 --> 00:16:50.700
There are three things we must protect.

230
00:16:51.070 --> 00:16:52.950
York's safety.

231
00:16:52.950 --> 00:16:55.410
The data stored inside Punk Records,

232
00:16:56.080 --> 00:16:59.040
and the power plant
that creates the Mother Flame.

233
00:16:59.580 --> 00:17:02.240
Everything else is expendable.

234
00:17:03.460 --> 00:17:07.550
But Sir, Rob Lucci and the other Cipher Pol agents
are still trapped inside there.

235
00:17:07.550 --> 00:17:09.880
We might face the worst case scenario.

236
00:17:10.430 --> 00:17:13.220
We must prioritize accordingly.

237
00:17:14.510 --> 00:17:18.270
Regard humans as you regard insects.

238
00:17:18.270 --> 00:17:20.890
Even if you exterminate
some, they'll multiply again.

239
00:17:26.360 --> 00:17:27.230
Yes, sir!

240
00:17:28.150 --> 00:17:30.530
You listen to me, you tiny terrorists!

241
00:17:30.530 --> 00:17:33.660
I made a pact with the Five Elders, you get it?

242
00:17:33.660 --> 00:17:36.910
Hurt me and you die!
What they do to this island

243
00:17:36.910 --> 00:17:38.790
will make Ohara look like fireworks! Huh?

244
00:17:49.090 --> 00:17:50.670
That hurt!

245
00:17:51.170 --> 00:17:52.550
You're gonna pay!

246
00:17:52.550 --> 00:17:54.550
I'll sic the Elders on you first!

247
00:17:54.550 --> 00:17:56.760
Yeah? Go right ahead!

248
00:17:57.140 --> 00:18:00.600
You're lucky that's all you got!
How dare you say that in front of Robin?!

249
00:18:00.600 --> 00:18:03.480
Keep your filthy mouth shut!

250
00:18:04.060 --> 00:18:06.190
She can't hurt us. Just ignore her.

251
00:18:07.150 --> 00:18:09.780
Robin, are you feeling okay?

252
00:18:09.780 --> 00:18:13.280
Of course. Have you met
my doctor? He's brilliant.

253
00:18:14.030 --> 00:18:16.490
That doesn't make me happy at all, you jerk!

254
00:18:18.910 --> 00:18:20.250
All things considered,
it was a pretty pathetic display!

255
00:18:20.620 --> 00:18:24.580
Though, to be fair,
I was fighting two Seraphim at once!

256
00:18:26.960 --> 00:18:28.170
You need to rest. You're hurt.

257
00:18:30.300 --> 00:18:32.300
Shaka!

258
00:18:32.300 --> 00:18:34.300
Pythagoras!

259
00:18:34.300 --> 00:18:35.680
Edison!

260
00:18:35.680 --> 00:18:38.310
Actually, I'm still alive.

261
00:18:38.310 --> 00:18:39.890
Oh, my God!

262
00:18:41.520 --> 00:18:43.640
Could you quiet down for a sec? What?

263
00:18:43.640 --> 00:18:46.610
I'm trying to get in contact
with the basement right now.

264
00:18:49.070 --> 00:18:52.110
Hey, can you guys hear me?
Everyone still alive?

265
00:18:52.110 --> 00:18:54.320
Thank you, Straw Hats!

266
00:18:55.320 --> 00:19:00.990
<b>Basement, Labophase</b>

267
00:18:55.740 --> 00:18:58.080
We can finally eat again!

268
00:18:58.080 --> 00:19:00.990
You saved us! We were losing hope!

269
00:19:00.990 --> 00:19:02.750
So good!

270
00:19:02.750 --> 00:19:04.120
I'm alive!

271
00:19:06.250 --> 00:19:08.380
Man, do I love the Straw Hat crew!

272
00:19:08.380 --> 00:19:10.500
Hey, not so loud, buddy!

273
00:19:10.500 --> 00:19:11.710
We're still enemies!

274
00:19:11.710 --> 00:19:14.380
Now is there any chance
he could let us out of this room?

275
00:19:14.380 --> 00:19:18.350
I'm glad all are okay, but we really
can't do that right now, sorry.

276
00:19:18.350 --> 00:19:20.930
Fair enough, but could you relocate us?

277
00:19:21.430 --> 00:19:25.560
It's kind of nerve wracking in here
with them around. What's wrong?

278
00:19:25.560 --> 00:19:27.480
Are you guys afraid of the Seraphim?

279
00:19:27.850 --> 00:19:30.480
They're supposed to be on the same
side as you guys,

280
00:19:30.480 --> 00:19:33.690
aren't they? Yeah,
but what if they go berserk?

281
00:19:33.690 --> 00:19:36.450
Hey, there's nothing to worry about, is there?

282
00:19:36.450 --> 00:19:37.660
No. They're safe.

283
00:19:38.030 --> 00:19:40.450
Those bubble balls are made
of the same material as

284
00:19:40.450 --> 00:19:44.710
the Pacifista Mk. III's Bubble Shields.

285
00:19:44.710 --> 00:19:47.120
They're resilient enough
to deflect cannon blasts.

286
00:19:47.460 --> 00:19:50.920
They are also created with sea energy,

287
00:19:50.920 --> 00:19:55.170
making them the perfect prison
to contain those with Devil Fruit powers.

288
00:19:55.170 --> 00:19:58.340
Oh, I thought they were just regular bubbles.

289
00:19:58.800 --> 00:20:01.300
How dare you trap me in this damn thing.

290
00:20:02.430 --> 00:20:04.810
It is foolish to be afraid of us.

291
00:20:04.810 --> 00:20:08.520
We do our job. And none
of the Seraphim were ordered to kill you!

292
00:20:09.020 --> 00:20:10.940
You're of no interest to us!

293
00:20:11.480 --> 00:20:13.150
Well then.

294
00:20:13.150 --> 00:20:15.240
Now I just feel silly.

295
00:20:15.610 --> 00:20:21.200
Don't mind the suits, S-Snake! They're just jumpy.
You're super cool in our book, after what you did before.

296
00:20:21.200 --> 00:20:24.450
Thanks for turning us back
from stone, little sister.

297
00:20:24.450 --> 00:20:26.330
She really did that?

298
00:20:26.330 --> 00:20:27.460
How peculiar.

299
00:20:27.460 --> 00:20:31.290
Unless I made an error, that behavior
should not lead her programming.

300
00:20:33.800 --> 00:20:35.300
Come on! Please, Hancock!

301
00:20:35.710 --> 00:20:37.300
They're my friends!

302
00:20:37.300 --> 00:20:38.840
You gotta undo this stone thing now!

303
00:20:39.510 --> 00:20:41.850
You're the only person who can save them!

304
00:20:41.850 --> 00:20:42.800
So please!

305
00:20:45.220 --> 00:20:47.390
Alright, fine!

306
00:20:47.390 --> 00:20:51.400
Let's do it! Just please stop
staring at me like that!

307
00:20:51.980 --> 00:20:54.150
Oh, I see how it is!

308
00:20:54.150 --> 00:20:59.150
She's just as unmanageable as the original Hancock!
With the same soft spot for Luffy!

309
00:20:59.150 --> 00:21:01.410
This is too funny!

310
00:21:02.240 --> 00:21:04.910
I didn't know Seraphim worked that way!

311
00:21:04.910 --> 00:21:07.200
– Ah!
– Oh, hi, Hancock!

312
00:21:07.200 --> 00:21:10.120
How's it going? Seems
the information transmitted

313
00:21:10.120 --> 00:21:12.790
through Blood Elements
is broader than I thought!

314
00:21:12.790 --> 00:21:14.250
Fascinating.

315
00:21:14.750 --> 00:21:17.760
You were super awesome
back there! I owe you!

316
00:21:17.760 --> 00:21:21.470
Did you just say "I love you"?

317
00:21:21.470 --> 00:21:22.590
What?

318
00:21:22.590 --> 00:21:24.970
Did you just say "I love you"?

319
00:21:31.510 --> 00:21:33.560
Hey, Stella, we've got trouble!

320
00:21:33.560 --> 00:21:36.440
The communication system's
been fully restored,

321
00:21:36.440 --> 00:21:39.320
but the Frontier Dome still
won't open for some reason!

322
00:21:40.570 --> 00:21:42.200
Don't even bother!

323
00:21:43.030 --> 00:21:45.410
I protected the Dome with a passcode,

324
00:21:45.410 --> 00:21:47.990
but my brain's not synced
with all of you anymore,

325
00:21:47.990 --> 00:21:49.750
and I'm not telling!

326
00:21:49.750 --> 00:21:51.500
Oh yeah?!

327
00:21:51.500 --> 00:21:53.790
Alright, I'll beat it out of you then!

328
00:21:53.790 --> 00:21:56.130
Lilith, no!

329
00:21:58.210 --> 00:22:01.220
While all of you lose
your minds, I'm gonna rest easy.

330
00:22:01.220 --> 00:22:03.680
Now go fetch me a snack.

331
00:22:03.730 --> 00:22:06.260
Snack on my fist, you pig!

332
00:22:06.260 --> 00:22:09.140
If we can't deactivate
the barrier, we can't escape.

333
00:22:09.140 --> 00:22:12.890
After all my smooth talking,
I thought we were free!

334
00:22:12.890 --> 00:22:14.900
Yeah, you're a real diplomat.

335
00:22:21.950 --> 00:22:24.030
Four seriously injured.

336
00:22:24.030 --> 00:22:26.950
Two of Vegapunk's satellites dead.

337
00:22:27.160 --> 00:22:29.290
As for the Straw Hats.

338
00:22:29.290 --> 00:22:31.750
You're mumbling. What's wrong?

339
00:22:33.000 --> 00:22:34.580
Just talking to myself.

340
00:22:36.960 --> 00:22:41.720
I checked outside and we're
completely surrounded in all directions.

341
00:22:41.720 --> 00:22:43.720
Hello, Stussy.

342
00:22:43.720 --> 00:22:47.930
It looks like 100 ships.
I'd assume there are around 30,000 Marines.

343
00:22:49.220 --> 00:22:50.680
My, this is quite the event.

344
00:22:50.680 --> 00:22:53.230
Welcome back, my darling.

345
00:22:53.230 --> 00:22:55.310
Care for a cup of coffee?

346
00:22:55.310 --> 00:22:56.400
Well, thank you.

347
00:22:58.230 --> 00:22:59.860
Stop glaring at me.

348
00:22:59.860 --> 00:23:03.150
You're Nami, correct? The crew's navigator?

349
00:23:03.150 --> 00:23:04.860
Uh huh, that's me!

350
00:23:04.860 --> 00:23:06.820
How does the route look?

351
00:23:06.820 --> 00:23:09.580
Eh. The Log Pose hasn't recorded a signal,

352
00:23:09.580 --> 00:23:12.040
but we still have
one steady needle from Wano.

353
00:23:12.410 --> 00:23:14.330
Seems we'll be going northeast.

354
00:23:14.330 --> 00:23:16.250
Ah, that would be Elbaf.

355
00:23:16.250 --> 00:23:18.460
– Really?
– Really?

356
00:23:18.460 --> 00:23:19.630
We're going?!

357
00:23:19.630 --> 00:23:20.960
Finally!

358
00:23:20.960 --> 00:23:22.340
Guess so. Yeah.

359
00:23:22.340 --> 00:23:24.130
And what's there?

360
00:23:25.330 --> 00:23:28.470
– The giants!
– The giants!

361
00:23:28.470 --> 00:23:31.810
Gia-gia-giants! Gia-gia-giants!

362
00:23:31.810 --> 00:23:34.560
Why are they so excited about this?

363
00:23:37.730 --> 00:23:39.650
We do have one advantage.

364
00:23:39.650 --> 00:23:43.110
Your ship is in the Labophase,
within our grasp.

365
00:23:43.610 --> 00:23:46.610
The Navy ships are offshore in all directions.

366
00:23:46.610 --> 00:23:49.070
It would be impossible to sail under the port!

367
00:23:49.570 --> 00:23:51.790
You said that we'll be heading
to the northeast.

368
00:23:52.160 --> 00:23:54.500
That's the backside of the island.

369
00:23:54.500 --> 00:23:58.120
Luckily, your ship is waiting right next
to the Vegaforce-01.

370
00:23:58.540 --> 00:24:03.590
With a little rocket propulsion,
it should be able to carry us clean over the Navy blockade.

371
00:24:03.590 --> 00:24:11.550
<b>Flight-Capable Airspace</b>

372
00:24:03.590 --> 00:24:08.090
On the downside, Vegaforce-01
can only fly within the airspace

373
00:24:08.090 --> 00:24:11.550
over Egghead. So let's hope we get
enough distance before we take a Norse dive.

374
00:24:11.550 --> 00:24:13.640
There's no way that'll be far enough!

375
00:24:13.640 --> 00:24:14.770
I got you,

376
00:24:14.770 --> 00:24:19.770
doc! You just do the best you can!
Then the Sunny's Coup de Burst will carry us the rest of the way!

377
00:24:19.770 --> 00:24:23.480
We'll fly a whole kilometer,
no way they'll catch us after that!

378
00:24:23.480 --> 00:24:24.860
My goodness!

379
00:24:24.860 --> 00:24:27.200
How in the world can your ship fly so far?!

380
00:24:27.200 --> 00:24:29.450
Cola power Vega-bro!

381
00:24:29.450 --> 00:24:30.950
Cola power?!

382
00:24:31.320 --> 00:24:32.530
Yeah!

383
00:24:40.000 --> 00:24:42.380
I love it! That sounds like a plan!

384
00:24:42.380 --> 00:24:43.860
Oh yeah!

385
00:24:44.000 --> 00:24:45.130
Lilith!

386
00:24:45.130 --> 00:24:47.130
Can you head to Vegaforce-01 now?

387
00:24:47.130 --> 00:24:48.630
I know what you're thinking!

388
00:24:48.630 --> 00:24:51.720
You want me to move the Straw Hat's ship
to the backside of the island, right?

389
00:24:52.220 --> 00:24:53.600
I'll help too!

390
00:24:53.600 --> 00:24:57.060
But we still can't go anywhere
till we deactivate the darn Frontier Dome.

391
00:24:57.060 --> 00:24:59.560
And I'm never gonna hand over the code!

392
00:25:07.110 --> 00:25:08.360
We'll crack it!

393
00:25:08.360 --> 00:25:10.870
– We'll crack the pumpkin!
– We'll crack the pumpkin!

394
00:25:12.070 --> 00:25:14.450
Seems like our plan is coming together nicely.

395
00:25:14.450 --> 00:25:18.540
I bet there's absolutely zero chance
we pull this off without a hitch.

396
00:25:20.040 --> 00:25:23.460
That's all we got.
And we don't know till we try.

397
00:25:23.460 --> 00:25:25.000
Yeah, that's true enough.

398
00:25:25.000 --> 00:25:28.970
If you're going to the Sunny, take me with!
That is my baby after all!

399
00:25:29.340 --> 00:25:30.470
Take me too!

400
00:25:30.470 --> 00:25:32.590
I can't wait to see Elbaf!

401
00:25:32.590 --> 00:25:33.930
Hey, let me help out!

402
00:25:34.430 --> 00:25:37.800
Thank you.

403
00:25:38.600 --> 00:25:40.270
Ready?

404
00:25:46.650 --> 00:25:50.030
Full speed ahead! It's time to go!

405
00:25:57.080 --> 00:25:59.120
Let's get your ship to the back side quick!

406
00:25:59.120 --> 00:26:01.620
They'll have that Frontier Dome down soon!

407
00:26:01.620 --> 00:26:04.710
That might be good! Or it might
just cause even more problems!

408
00:26:04.710 --> 00:26:07.090
I don't get it.
Why wouldn't you want it down?

409
00:26:07.090 --> 00:26:10.550
Cause there's a catch.
If we can get out, the Feds can get in!

410
00:26:10.550 --> 00:26:13.890
If we're not ready to rock
when it opens, we're in trouble!

411
00:26:13.890 --> 00:26:15.510
Oh, I see now.

412
00:26:15.510 --> 00:26:19.850
This is so much fun! I've never left
Egghead! World, here I come!

413
00:26:19.850 --> 00:26:22.490
Come on, Doc! This ain't a road trip!

414
00:26:23.140 --> 00:26:24.690
I just thought of something.

415
00:26:26.150 --> 00:26:28.400
We're gonna need so much more food!

416
00:26:28.400 --> 00:26:29.480
Oh, yeah, you're right!

417
00:26:29.900 --> 00:26:32.240
We'd eat all of this in one day!
Do we even have pizzas?

418
00:26:32.240 --> 00:26:33.700
Crack. That's super important!

419
00:26:33.700 --> 00:26:35.700
We have to get a ton of cheese!

420
00:26:35.700 --> 00:26:38.330
I think we have everything else
Sanji needs to make them for us.

421
00:26:38.890 --> 00:26:41.700
Really? That guy's pretty cool, huh?!

422
00:26:41.700 --> 00:26:43.540
He's a good cook and a good fighter!

423
00:26:43.540 --> 00:26:44.790
Huh.

424
00:26:44.790 --> 00:26:48.750
This is weird! What's got you
in such a happy mood all of a sudden?

425
00:26:48.750 --> 00:26:51.920
Earlier, you wanted to kill Old Man Apple.

426
00:26:56.550 --> 00:27:00.380
You're right, I did. But I'm over that now.

427
00:27:01.930 --> 00:27:05.020
That's good. So why
were you crying all night?

428
00:27:05.020 --> 00:27:06.900
Hey, shut up! I was not!

429
00:27:08.270 --> 00:27:10.070
We received a transmission from Lucci.

430
00:27:10.610 --> 00:27:13.400
We know the situation inside the dome now.

431
00:27:16.660 --> 00:27:18.660
Share it with the other ships!

432
00:27:18.660 --> 00:27:19.450
Yes, sir!

433
00:27:26.120 --> 00:27:28.750
Did you hear that, Borsalino?

434
00:27:29.750 --> 00:27:30.960
Uh huh.

435
00:27:31.590 --> 00:27:35.880
He talked a big game, but it seems he doesn't
have quite as much leverage as implied.

436
00:27:35.880 --> 00:27:39.970
In fact, all of them are trapped
in that Dome like rats.

437
00:27:39.970 --> 00:27:44.020
If it uses a laser defense system, can't you simply

438
00:27:44.020 --> 00:27:46.270
pass through it? You are light itself,

439
00:27:46.270 --> 00:27:47.520
are you not?

440
00:27:47.520 --> 00:27:50.020
Well, the barrier isn't what's stopping me.

441
00:27:50.020 --> 00:27:54.240
There's a friend of mine waiting on the shore,
and he wants to protect Vegapunk.

442
00:27:54.240 --> 00:27:56.360
Why not fly over him?

443
00:27:56.360 --> 00:28:02.080
I can't disrespect a man who's putting everything on the line.
I like to think I'm cooler than that.

444
00:28:02.580 --> 00:28:05.790
At the very least, let
me stick to my principles.

445
00:28:06.250 --> 00:28:10.250
And remember, Sentomaru is poised
to attack The second we make

446
00:28:10.250 --> 00:28:16.550
a move, he'll order every resource at his command into action.
That means a swarm of Sea Beast Weapons and fifty Pacifistas.

447
00:28:16.550 --> 00:28:19.970
Bad news for all the ships we brought.

448
00:28:19.970 --> 00:28:23.560
We'll be committing to a massive bloodbath.

449
00:28:25.180 --> 00:28:27.020
We better settle this quickly.

450
00:28:28.140 --> 00:28:30.230
Do we know where the power plant is?

451
00:28:34.480 --> 00:28:38.110
Our friend Lucci
hasn't been sleeping on the job.

452
00:28:38.110 --> 00:28:43.660
We have all the information we need.
And he delivered it straight to our door.

453
00:28:53.500 --> 00:28:56.690
– Prepare for battle!
– Prepare for battle!

454
00:28:56.690 --> 00:28:59.220
Prepare for battle!

455
00:28:59.590 --> 00:29:03.180
Six Power Masters proceed
to land as soon as the battle begins!

456
00:29:03.180 --> 00:29:06.890
Our mission is to free
the captured Cipher Pol agents!

457
00:29:07.480 --> 00:29:10.770
Artillery fire won't work on the Pacifistas!

458
00:29:10.770 --> 00:29:14.230
Aim all cannons at the Sea Beast Weapons!

459
00:29:24.370 --> 00:29:26.620
This sure is fun!

460
00:29:26.620 --> 00:29:29.140
Just like on Sky Island!

461
00:29:31.170 --> 00:29:35.490
I love this place too.
But we gotta lock in, bro.

462
00:29:35.840 --> 00:29:36.550
Made it!

463
00:29:36.550 --> 00:29:38.210
There's the Sunny!

464
00:29:47.890 --> 00:29:49.600
No turning back.

465
00:29:49.600 --> 00:29:54.760
Sacred Yata Mirror!

466
00:30:11.080 --> 00:30:13.420
He's here. Let's go!

467
00:30:13.420 --> 00:30:15.420
Pacifistas!

468
00:30:31.140 --> 00:30:34.600
I won't go easy on you, Sentomaru!

469
00:30:37.150 --> 00:30:39.110
Bring it on, uncle!

470
00:30:40.030 --> 00:30:42.740
You're facing the strongest defense.

471
00:30:43.700 --> 00:30:46.820
in the whole world!

472
00:30:56.830 --> 00:30:58.340
What?

473
00:30:58.340 --> 00:30:59.550
What's going on?

474
00:30:59.920 --> 00:31:01.760
Where is this light coming from?

475
00:31:05.010 --> 00:31:06.720
Someone's here!

476
00:31:07.550 --> 00:31:09.010
Someone strong!

477
00:31:16.680 --> 00:31:21.770
Running so long lost track of just how long its been

478
00:31:22.620 --> 00:31:29.130
Collected scars while striving not even trying beneath my skin

479
00:31:29.630 --> 00:31:36.550
But in the back of my head the dream is not dead I remember a map

480
00:31:36.630 --> 00:31:42.840
to a treasure still gleaming its within our grasp

481
00:31:42.980 --> 00:31:49.750
Can you feel my heart Feelings I impart

482
00:31:49.710 --> 00:31:56.860
The promises are there theyre deep down but still primed to share

483
00:31:56.990 --> 00:32:05.970
Peerless dreams kept close the dreams that always matter most

484
00:32:06.150 --> 00:32:11.720
Before we set sail why not raise a toast

485
00:32:11.840 --> 00:32:18.750
So I pen this note to you Dear sunrise Ill see you soon

486
00:32:18.910 --> 00:32:25.940
See the smile I saw the day that I sang this song to you

487
00:32:25.920 --> 00:32:32.990
And regardless of our age these memries will still remain

488
00:32:32.890 --> 00:32:40.100
Wont forget until this wish makes it to you
